I disagree.  I just ran some wizard mode tests.  The first set of tests
were with a +0 uncursed broad pick at expert skill.  The second set of
tests were with a stack of +0 uncursed daggers at basic skill.  In
every single test, I lost more HP when I used daggers.

The important thing here is that a +0 broad pick at expert level
usually kills an energy vortex in 2 hits, and if the RNG hates you then
it might take 3 hits to kill an energy vortex.  It is also important to
note that you don't get shocked when you make the killing blow.  This
means that you'll usually get shocked only once from using a wielded
weapon.

However, +0 daggers at basic skill take a very long time to kill an
energy vortex, and the energy vortex is repeatedly doing its normal
shock damage to you while you slowly kill it with daggers.  Thus, an
archeologist is better off using a broad pick against an energy vortex.



